cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  A DOI will be added here once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
type: software
title: >-
  deppro: depth-composition reconstruction from angle-resolved X-ray
  photoelectron spectroscopy
authors:
  - family-names: Toyoda
    given-names: Satoshi
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1091-1579'
    affiliation: >-
      Office of Institutional Advancement and Communications,
      Kyoto University, Kyoto, Japan
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-02'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/stoyoda0012-cyber/depthprofiler'
abstract: >-
  deppro reconstructs depth profiles of composition in thin films from
  angle-resolved X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (ARXPS) and hard X-ray
  photoelectron spectroscopy (HAXPES) intensities. It builds a transfer
  matrix from inelastic mean free paths and the measurement geometry and
  inverts it under physical constraints and regularisation, with reference
  CPU solvers, batched solvers on Apple-silicon GPUs (MLX) and a
  neural-network inverse solver.
keywords:
  - XPS
  - HAXPES
  - ARXPS
  - photoelectron spectroscopy
  - depth profiling
  - inverse problem
  - Apple Silicon
  - MLX
